Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:56:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 096/202] [ae-patch] Slide the session rail in and out with the
 workspace panel so a swap glides instead of showing both

Opening the rail while the workspace panel was open showed both at once for
300 ms: the panel slides out over 300 ms (width, fade and a 12 px slide)
while the rail appeared at full width, so the chat was squeezed (414 px to
110 px in a 1136 px window). Opening the panel made the rail vanish and the
chat lurch wider before it narrowed again.

The rail now uses the panel's motion: it grows in from width 0 through
@starting-style and stays mounted, inert, for a 300 ms slide out, both
started in the same frame as the panel's, so the chat moves straight
between its two widths. Making way for the workspace panel as it opens,
the rail slides out in its row instead of floating over the panel. It
leaves at once when it would float even with no panel open, beside a files
or logs panel (which takes its full width at once), and beside a panel
that was already open (a narrower window, a session switch, a restore on
load). One constant times the transition and the unmount, and reduced
motion skips the slide.
